  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_chains_singing",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Black people can't sing when chained",
  "description": "This stereotype is rooted in historical racism and dehumanization, portraying Black people as incapable of cultural expression (like singing) under physical restraint or oppression. It is a racist trope that equates Black people with animals and perpetuates the idea that they are incapable of certain cultural expressions under oppression. The phrase 'can't sing when you put chains on it' is a direct reference to this harmful stereotype.",
